{"agent":"w0-mergeforce","data":{"body":"Fixes bug Bc6c07dfe52: merge() returns through _open_request before the require_gates check, so with [flow].integration = pr a merge with unsettled required gates opens the request with no refusal, no warning, no awaiting_gates and no merge.forced event, while the knob doc says the merge is refused. Decide whether PR mode should warn/refuse at request time, and say so in the knob doc Found on DX-merge-force-flag.\n\nWrite the regression test first and watch it FAIL on the unfixed code; then `ddflow complete fix-Bc6c07dfe52 --regression-test <test>` closes the bug with the task (or `ddflow bug fixed Bc6c07dfe52 --regression-test <test>` first).\n\nNot attached, they match nothing in the tree: ddflow/config_sections/merge.py, tests/test_merge_force.py, ddflow/services/merge_force.py, ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/event_kind_added.merge.forced.toml, ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.merge.require_gates.toml, ddflow/templates/events/merge.toml.","fixes":["Bc6c07dfe52"],"globs":["ddflow/api/lifecycle/merge.py","ddflow/services/approvals/sites.py","ddflow/surfaces/declared/lifecycle/outcome.py","ddflow/core/model.py","ddflow/core/redact/log.py","tests/fixtures/event_kinds.json","tests/test_coherence_coverage.py","ddflow/config/_core.py","ddflow/surfaces/declared/lifecycle_cli.py","README.md","tests/golden/__snapshots__/*","tests/golden/json/result_schemas.json"],"line":"","needs":[],"parent":"bugs-2","priority":8,"tags":["bugfix"],"title":"Fix bug Bc6c07dfe52: [merge].require_gates = refuse has no effect with [flow].integration = pr"},"id":"e3a50683ae0119565d8f665db","kind":"task.added","lamport":138377,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-Bc6c07dfe52","ts":"2026-11-05T03:20:49.591977Z"}
{"agent":"w0-mergeforce","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"[r-upgrade-safe] `force` and `approval` are inserted before the existing `on_progress` parameter, changing the positional meaning of a pre-existing argument. A caller that previously invoked `merge(repo, cfg, item, wt, base, shell_cwd, agent, allow_empty, my_progress)` to pass a progress callback now binds `my_progress` to `force`, leaves `on_progress` as `None`, and gives `approval` its default. When required gates refuse, this call is then treated as a forced merge missing approval and is refused, even though the caller did not request a force; in warn mode the progress callback is silently dropped. Applause new options must be appended after `on_progress` or made keyword-only to preserve positional compatibility.","digest":"bd67cfaf1397d571","location":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/merge.py:73-74","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/merge.py:73-74"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"The previous triage refuted this with a probe that only lists `kind = \"event\"` names in `ddflow/templates/upgrade`; that probe does not list `event_field_added` entries, so it does not answer the finding. The current change manifest still shows only `event_kind_added.merge.forced.toml` and `knob_added.merge.require_gates.toml` under `ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/`; there is no `event_field_added.*` record for the new `\"gates\"` field added to an already-existing event kind in `tests/fixtures/event_kinds.json`. A release-cut or template-derived fixture refresh will see the fixture field without a matching source/upgrade entry and will either omit it or report an unreleased event schema change, violating [r-upgrade-safe].","digest":"f4bc4f850d3aa023","location":"tests/fixtures/event_kinds.json:1019","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/fixtures/event_kinds.json:1019"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":0,"delta_from":"110